            <ArticleTitle>CB-Receptor Agonist HU-210 Mimics the Postconditioning Phenomenon of Isolated Heart.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-29</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>CB receptor agonist HU-210 exhibits an infarction-limiting effect during in vitro reperfusion of the heart after focal ischemia. This effect is paralleled by a decrease in left-ventricular developed pressure and double product. In addition, HU-210 reduces end-diastolic pressure during the reperfusion period, which indirectly attests to reduced Ca(2+) overload of cardiomyocytes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
